The interactions between TSH, HCG, and GnRH have significant clinical implications, particularly in the diagnosis and treatment of endocrine disorders. For example, low TSH levels in patients with anorexia nervosa can indicate thyroid axis alterations, while HCG's role in stimulating testosterone production is critical for treating male hypogonadism. Understanding these relationships is essential for healthcare providers in managing hormonal imbalances and related health issues. [Data: Relationships (8731, 11106, 12301)]# Williams Textbook of Endocrinology Community

