Testosterone treatment can lead to several potential adverse effects, including erythrocytosis and endometrial atrophy. Erythrocytosis, characterized by an increase in red blood cells, can pose health risks for patients undergoing testosterone therapy. Additionally, endometrial atrophy may occur in transsexual men receiving testosterone, indicating the need for careful monitoring of treatment outcomes. Understanding these risks is crucial for healthcare providers when considering testosterone therapy for patients. [Data: Entities (5445, 5446); Relationships (14880, 14881)]

