Neuroendocrine tumors (TUMORES NEUROENDOCRINOS) are closely associated with MEN syndromes, particularly MEN1. These tumors can arise from neuroendocrine cells and may lead to significant health issues, including chronic diarrhea and hormonal imbalances. The relationship between MEN1 and neuroendocrine tumors is critical, as these tumors represent one of the primary causes of mortality among affected patients, underscoring the importance of monitoring and managing these conditions. [Data: Entities (3629), Relationships (12023, 12024, 12030)]

