VIPOMA is a type of pancreatic neuroendocrine tumor characterized by the secretion of vasoactive intestinal peptide (VIP), leading to severe diarrhea and electrolyte imbalances. This condition highlights the functional impact of pancreatic tumors on the body's homeostasis. The relationship between VIPOMA and the pancreas is critical, as the tumor's origin directly affects treatment options and patient management. [Data: Entities (5756); Relationships (14006, 15164)]

