The Complejo de Carney can affect various endocrine glands, including the pituitary gland, leading to the development of tumors. This can result in hormonal imbalances and a range of clinical symptoms that require careful monitoring and management. The relationship between the syndrome and the pituitary gland underscores the importance of regular medical evaluations for individuals diagnosed with Complejo de Carney. [Data: Relationships (11859)]

