DHEA-S levels are often elevated in cases of hyperandrogenism, establishing a direct relationship between this hormone and conditions characterized by excessive androgen levels. This connection is particularly relevant in the context of Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS), where DHEA-S plays a role in the hormonal imbalance observed in affected individuals. [Data: Entities (4955); Relationships (14383, 12722)]

