Parinaud syndrome is a collection of neurological symptoms that can occur in patients with tumors in the pineal region, indicating the need for careful neurological evaluation. One of the hallmark symptoms of this syndrome is the paralysis of upward gaze, which can severely affect a patient's quality of life. The presence of this syndrome in patients with pineal tumors underscores the critical nature of timely diagnosis and intervention. [Data: Entities (3783); Relationships (12591)]

