Constitutional delay is a temporary condition affecting growth and development, often delaying puberty. It is important to differentiate this condition from pathological causes of primary amenorrhea to avoid unnecessary interventions. The relationship between constitutional delay and primary amenorrhea underscores the complexity of diagnosing developmental issues in children. [Data: Entities (5312), Relationships (14805)]

