Insulin resistance is a key characteristic of Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2, leading to elevated blood glucose levels and contributing to the development of various metabolic disorders. This condition is often linked to obesity and is a significant risk factor for cardiovascular disease. Understanding insulin resistance is essential for developing effective treatment strategies for DM2 and related health issues. [Data: Entities (4153); Relationships (12887, 13230)]

