Lifestyle choices, including diet and physical activity, play a crucial role in managing Diabetes Mellitus Tipo 2. Adherence to a Mediterranean diet has been shown to reduce the risk of developing DM2, highlighting the importance of dietary interventions. Additionally, lifestyle modifications are essential for managing comorbidities such as dyslipidemia and hypertension, emphasizing the need for patient education and support. [Data: Entities (9255, 11532); Relationships (11532, 13255)]

