Creta is renowned for its traditional Mediterranean diet, which is linked to lower rates of coronary heart disease. The island's dietary practices, characterized by high intake of alpha-linolenic acid, contribute to its health outcomes. The PREDIMED study includes findings related to Creta, emphasizing the importance of traditional diets in understanding the relationship between nutrition and cardiovascular health [Data: Entities (10807); Relationships (15527)].# Cardiovascular Health and Dietary Fats

