Hipercalciuria is a condition characterized by excessive calcium in the urine, which significantly increases the risk of developing kidney stones. This condition can lead to the formation of c√°lculos renales, as the elevated calcium levels contribute to the concentration of salts in the urine, facilitating stone formation. The relationship between hipercalciuria and kidney stones is well-documented, indicating that individuals with hipercalciuria are at a higher risk for developing renal calculi. [Data: Entities (11939), Relationships (15210, 18918)]

