## Interactions between alcohol and medications

Alcohol can interact negatively with various medications, enhancing their effects or leading to adverse reactions. For example, alcohol can potentiate the effects of antidepressants and beta-blockers, which may lead to increased side effects or reduced efficacy of these medications. This underscores the need for caution among patients who are prescribed these drugs and consume alcohol [Data: Relationships (11276, 11279, 11275, 14235, 14234, +more)].

