GLUT4 is a glucose transporter protein essential for insulin-regulated glucose uptake in muscle and fat tissues. Its regulation is particularly important in the context of Diabetes Type 2 management, as it directly affects glucose metabolism. Understanding the function of GLUT4 can lead to better therapeutic strategies aimed at improving insulin sensitivity and overall glucose control. [Data: Entities (4169), Relationships (13284)]

