Calcium and Vitamin D play a significant role in dietary management, particularly for individuals with lactose intolerance. These nutrients are essential for preventing bone density loss, which can be a concern for those unable to consume dairy products. Dietary recommendations emphasize the inclusion of calcium and Vitamin D supplements to support overall health, highlighting the importance of these nutrients in the context of dietary management for specific health conditions [Data: Entities (9738); Relationships (17935, +more)].# Flavonoids and Their Health Implications

